# 🚀 Apache Spark / PySpark Cheat Sheet

> 📚 A quick reference for the most commonly used Apache Spark & PySpark commands used in **Data Engineering**, **Big Data**, and **Interview Preparation**.

## 🏗️ Spark Session

| 🛠️ Command | 💻 Syntax | 📖 Definition |
|------------|-----------|---------------|
| `SparkSession.builder.getOrCreate()` | `spark = SparkSession.builder.appName("App").getOrCreate()` | Creates and initializes a Spark application. |

---

## 📂 Reading Data

| 🛠️ Command | 💻 Syntax | 📖 Definition |
|------------|-----------|---------------|
| `read.csv()` | `spark.read.csv(path)` | Reads CSV files into a DataFrame. |
| `read.parquet()` | `spark.read.parquet(path)` | Reads Parquet files into a DataFrame. |
| `read.json()` | `spark.read.json(path)` | Reads JSON files into a DataFrame. |
| `read.orc()` | `spark.read.orc(path)` | Reads ORC files into a DataFrame. |

---

## 👀 Exploring Data

| 🛠️ Command | 💻 Syntax | 📖 Definition |
|------------|-----------|---------------|
| `show()` | `df.show()` | Displays the first 20 rows. |
| `printSchema()` | `df.printSchema()` | Displays DataFrame schema. |
| `columns` | `df.columns` | Returns all column names. |
| `count()` | `df.count()` | Returns total number of records. |
| `describe()` | `df.describe()` | Displays summary statistics. |
| `limit()` | `df.limit(10)` | Returns the first *n* rows. |

---

## 🎯 Selecting & Filtering

| 🛠️ Command | 💻 Syntax | 📖 Definition |
|------------|-----------|---------------|
| `select()` | `df.select("Name","Salary")` | Selects required columns. |
| `selectExpr()` | `df.selectExpr("Salary*12 AS AnnualSalary")` | Selects using SQL expressions. |
| `filter()` | `df.filter(df.Salary > 50000)` | Filters rows based on conditions. |
| `where()` | `df.where("Salary > 50000")` | SQL-style filtering. |

---

## ✨ Column Operations

| 🛠️ Command | 💻 Syntax | 📖 Definition |
|------------|-----------|---------------|
| `withColumn()` | `df.withColumn("Bonus", col("Salary")*0.1)` | Adds or modifies a column. |
| `withColumnRenamed()` | `df.withColumnRenamed("Salary","MonthlySalary")` | Renames a column. |
| `drop()` | `df.drop("Age")` | Removes columns. |
| `cast()` | `col("Salary").cast("int")` | Converts data type. |
| `alias()` | `col("Salary").alias("MonthlySalary")` | Creates an alias. |

---

## 🔍 Sorting & Removing Duplicates

| 🛠️ Command | 💻 Syntax | 📖 Definition |
|------------|-----------|---------------|
| `orderBy()` | `df.orderBy("Salary")` | Sorts ascending. |
| `sort()` | `df.sort(df.Salary.desc())` | Sorts ascending/descending. |
| `distinct()` | `df.distinct()` | Removes duplicate rows. |
| `dropDuplicates()` | `df.dropDuplicates()` | Removes duplicate rows based on columns. |

---

## 📊 Aggregations

| 🛠️ Command | 💻 Syntax | 📖 Definition |
|------------|-----------|---------------|
| `groupBy()` | `df.groupBy("Department")` | Groups records. |
| `agg()` | `df.groupBy("Department").agg(sum("Salary"))` | Performs aggregation. |
| `sum()` | `sum("Salary")` | Calculates total. |
| `avg()` | `avg("Salary")` | Calculates average. |
| `min()` | `min("Salary")` | Returns minimum value. |
| `max()` | `max("Salary")` | Returns maximum value. |

